wifi: mt76: mt7996: send the STA_REC before the per-station VoW setup

Backport of upstream openwrt/mt76 commit da2c90d2 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996:
send the STA_REC before the per-station VoW setup") to the mt76 revision
pinned by OpenWrt 25.12 (PKG_SOURCE_VERSION 39c960c3, 2026-03-19).

The upstream commit was written against a later revision where
mt7996_mcu_add_group() had been renamed to mt7996_mcu_sta_init_vow() and
took &link->mt76 instead of link. At 39c960c3 the equivalent code is
mt7996_mcu_add_group(), which sends UNI_VOW_DRR_CTRL through
MCU_WM_UNI_CMD(VOW). The bug and the fix are identical.

Problem: in mt7996_mcu_add_sta() the VoW/DRR group request was issued
*before* the STA_REC_UPDATE, and a failure of that request caused the
already-built STA_REC skb to be freed:

	ret = mt7996_mcu_add_group(dev, link, wcid);
	if (ret) {
		dev_kfree_skb(skb);     <-- STA_REC never reaches firmware
		return ret;
	}
out:
	return mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(&dev->mt76, skb,
				     MCU_WMWA_UNI_CMD(STA_REC_UPDATE), true);

The firmware rejects the per-station VoW request with status 0xc0000001
("GetDisablePerStaTx Failed" in the firmware log) when it has no station
record for that wcid yet. That happens for every new association after a
full interface teardown/rebuild (e.g. `wifi down` + `wifi up`, or any
netifd interface restart), because the teardown wipes the firmware STA
context. The result is that the STA_REC update is never sent, so clients
can never associate again - and `wifi reload` cannot recover it, only a
reboot can.

Fix: send the STA_REC update first, and only then program the VoW/DRR
group. A failing VoW no longer discards the STA_REC skb, and is ignored
(returning an error here would make mac80211 tear the station down again
even though it is already registered in firmware).

Tested on Cudy TR3600 v1 (MT7987 + MT7996): after the change, `wifi
down; wifi up` no longer breaks client association, and the firmware log
no longer shows the failed per-STA TX setup.

Signed-off-by: TR3600 build kit <noreply@example.com>
---
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -2718,14 +2718,21 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	ret = mt7996_mcu_add_group(dev, link, wcid);
-	if (ret) {
-		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
-		return ret;
-	}
 out:
-	return mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(&dev->mt76, skb,
-				     MCU_WMWA_UNI_CMD(STA_REC_UPDATE), true);
+	ret = mt76_mcu_skb_send_msg(&dev->mt76, skb,
+				    MCU_WMWA_UNI_CMD(STA_REC_UPDATE), true);
+	if (ret || conn_state == CONN_STATE_DISCONNECT)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * The firmware rejects the per-station VoW/DRR request for a wcid it
+	 * has no station record for yet (seen right after a wifi down/up
+	 * cycle). Sending the STA_REC update first guarantees the station is
+	 * registered, and a failing VoW no longer discards the STA_REC skb.
+	 */
+	mt7996_mcu_add_group(dev, link, wcid);
+
+	return 0;
 }
 
 int mt7996_mcu_teardown_mld_sta(struct mt7996_dev *dev,
